.TH RSETUP-NEXT 1 "2026-09-04" "rsetup-next 0.5.0-alpha.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rsetup-next \- local control center for Linux single-board computers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rsetup-next
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ COMMAND-OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rsetup-next
provides device inspection, guided system operations, APT source management,
an interactive terminal interface, and a loopback Web control center.
Mutating operations are dry-run by default.
Root-required live operations from an unprivileged interface use a fixed-action
Polkit helper; the application itself remains unprivileged.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the current device snapshot.
.TP
.B actions
List guided operations.
.TP
.B run ACTION
Preview or execute a catalog action.
.TP
.B sources COMMAND
Inspect, plan, or apply APT source changes.
.TP
.B hardware COMMAND
Inspect and manage overlays, the 40-pin GPIO map, cameras, thermal policy,
temperature-driven fan curves, LEDs, and SPI boot flash. Mutations require
explicit confirmation.
.PP
The GPIO map matches the SBC against an embedded catalog of 20 pinout profiles
and reports at most one current function per physical pin. Running functions
require evidence from debugfs pinctrl or read-only
.BR gpioinfo (1)
metadata. Saved Overlay files under
.I /boot
describe the configured next boot, not the current pinmux. Missing evidence is
reported as unconfirmed; status inspection does not invoke
.BR gpioget (1)
or request a GPIO line.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the current runtime and execution policy.
.TP
.B tui
Start the interactive terminal interface.
.TP
.B serve
Start the Web control center on the loopback interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Use synthetic SBC data.
.TP
.B \-\-live-execution
Allow live mutation on Linux. Confirmation and root checks still apply.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " LANGUAGE"
Select automatic, English, or Simplified Chinese presentation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rsetup-next status --json
rsetup-next --demo tui
rsetup-next sources plan cqu
rsetup-next hardware overlays status
rsetup-next hardware gpio --json
rsetup-next hardware leds status
rsetup-next hardware spi-flash status
rsetup-next hardware spi-flash plan install mtd0 \
  --image rock-5b-rk3588:rockchip-rk35
rsetup-next hardware video capture video0 --output camera.jpg
rsetup-next hardware thermal set step_wise --confirm
rsetup-next hardware thermal fan-curve status --json
rsetup-next hardware thermal fan-curve plan --zone thermal_zone0 \
  --device cooling_device0 --point 40:20 --point 55:45 \
  --point 70:75 --point 82:100 --json
sudo rsetup-next --live-execution hardware thermal fan-curve apply \
  --zone thermal_zone0 --device cooling_device0 \
  --point 40:20 --point 55:45 --point 70:75 --point 82:100 \
  --plan-token TOKEN --confirm
sudo rsetup-next --live-execution sources apply cqu \
  --plan-token TOKEN --confirm
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list
Traditional APT source configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/
Traditional and Deb822 APT source configuration fragments.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/rsetup-next-helper
Polkit-authorized helper for fixed catalog operations.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/com.radxa.rsetup-next.policy
Authorization policy for the privileged helper.
.TP
.I /etc/rsetup-next/thermal-policy
Validated thermal policy restored at boot.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/rsetup-next-thermal-policy.service
Oneshot thermal-policy restore unit.
.TP
.I /etc/rsetup-next/fan-curve.json
Root-only curve configuration, including the preserved previous governor.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/rsetup-next-fan-curve.service
Temperature-driven controller. Sensor failure, fatal error, SIGTERM, and
ExecStop force maximum cooling; deliberate disable restores the prior governor.
.TP
.I /run/lock/rsetup-next-fan-curve.lock
Exclusive lock held across final plan revalidation and curve mutation.
.TP
.I /etc/rsetup-next/led-state.json
Saved LED trigger and RGB pattern state.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/rsetup-next-led-state.service
Oneshot LED-state restore unit.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/u-boot/
Trusted installed bootloader assets used to assemble compatible SPI images.
.TP
.I /var/lib/rsetup-next/spi-backups/
Root-only recovery images captured before SPI flash changes.
.TP
.I /sys/kernel/debug/pinctrl/*/pinmux-pins
Runtime pinmux evidence used when debugfs is available and readable.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/rsetup-next/PINOUT_PROVENANCE.md
Source commit, license, and regeneration instructions for the normalized
20-profile pinout catalog.
.SH NOTES
The pinout snapshot is derived from
.I xzl01/pin-out
with copyright-owner authorization for distribution under GPL-3.0-or-later.
Runtime pinctrl and read-only GPIO metadata still require validation across
real SBCs; absent evidence is intentionally left unconfirmed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RSETUP_EXECUTION
Set to
.B live
to opt into live execution.
.TP
.B RSETUP_LANG
Select the presentation language.
.TP
.B RSETUP_MODE
Select automatic, live, or demo probing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt-get (8),
.BR gpioinfo (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
